# Pairs with UniqueOwner. Retiring the old copy clears its Rejecting phase
# instead of keeping it, so a router whose cached pair names T is served by T
# again while the alias names R.
MODULE: UniqueOwnerRetireLiftsFence
TARGET: UniqueOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: retiring the old copy lifts its fence, so a stale router is served by it again
PERTURBS: ResizeRetire

--- FIND
ResizeRetire ==
    /\ rz = "swapped"
    /\ fence' = rzShards
--- REPLACE
ResizeRetire ==
    /\ rz = "swapped"
\* MUTATION: the fence is cleared at retirement.
    /\ fence' = {}
--- END